      "date": "2026-09-03 11:53:46.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(4 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nThe one-line change is correct: llmountcleanup.sh -> cleanupall -f -> unload_modules_local() -> \"$LUSTRE_RMMOD ldiskfs\" takes the \"${modules[*]}\" == \"ldiskfs\" branch, so the edited fallback list is the one that runs, and ec.ko has no in-kernel dependents (its four EXPORT_SYMBOL()s are used only by lustre/kunit/ec_test.c and by userspace liblustreapi), so a dependency walk never reaches it. The commit message needs a refresh though - subject tag and a Fixes: line; the inline nit can ride along.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
